## 2026-07-29 — Global Search Command Palette

**Task:** Add a global search across all writeup categories (pentest-labs, walkthroughs, ctf).
**Decision:** Command palette (Ctrl+K / Cmd+K) in the navbar. Client-side filtering on title + tags. No external search lib — simple `filter` + `includes` is sufficient for ~25 writeups. Results grouped by category, direct navigation to writeup on click.
**Alternatives considered:**
- Inline search field always visible in navbar (rejected: takes too much space)
- Full-text search on MDX body (rejected: user chose title + tags only)
- Fuse.js / Algolia (rejected: overkill for current volume)
**Files changed:** `lib/content.ts` (new `getAllWriteups()`), `components/SearchDialog.tsx` (new), `components/Header.tsx` (integration), `dictionaries/fr.json` + `en.json` (search keys), `components/ui/dialog.tsx` (shadcn install).
**Status:** Active

---

## 2026-08-08 - Build-Time Indexing and Category Filtering Optimizations

**Task:** Improve content loading performance (solve I/O bottleneck) and enhance UI/UX with search, category filtering, lazy-loaded screenshots, pagination, and related recommendations.
**Decision:**
- Created a Node script `scripts/generate-index.js` that compiles all MDX frontmatter metadata (including calculated reading time and platform attributes) into a single `content/index.json` during build and development.
- Modified `lib/content.ts` to load listing views from `index.json` in-memory.
- Created `components/CategoryList.tsx` (client component) providing real-time client-side search, platform filter, tag filters, featured posts grid (latest 3 posts), and client-side pagination.
- Added custom MDX `img` component mapping standard markdown images to stylized, lazy-loaded screenshots to prevent CLS.
- Added similar article suggestions using tag overlap correlation.
**Alternatives considered:**
- Physical image files conversion to WebP/AVIF (rejected by user preference).
- Fuse.js / client-side search library (rejected: client-side filter is faster and zero-dependency for ~30 posts).
**Status:** Active

